{
  "$schema": "/scene-schema.json",
  "id": "trie",
  "title": "Trie (Prefix Tree)",
  "type": "lld",
  "layout": "text-left-canvas-right",
  "description": "See how a Trie (Prefix Tree) enables O(m) search, insert, and startsWith — where m is the word length. Powers autocomplete in every search bar you've used.",
  "category": "Low Level Design",
  "canvas": [
    {
      "id": "trie-tree",
      "type": "tree",
      "variant": "trie",
      "layoutHint": "tree-RT",
      "label": "Trie Structure  (* = end of word)",
      "initialState": {
        "nodes": [
          { "id": "root", "value": "·", "children": [], "isEnd": false }
        ],
        "rootId": "root"
      }
    }
  ],
  "activeText": {
    "initialValue": "Empty Trie  —  root node (·) represents start"
  },
  "controls": [
    {
      "id": "btn-insert-app",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "insert('app')",
      "config": {
        "variant": "primary",
        "goToStep": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "btn-insert-apple",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "insert('apple')",
      "config": {
        "variant": "primary",
        "goToStep": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "btn-insert-ban",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "insert('ban')",
      "config": {
        "variant": "primary",
        "goToStep": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "btn-search-app",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "search('app') ✓",
      "config": {
        "variant": "secondary",
        "goToStep": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "btn-starts-ap",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "startsWith('ap') ✓",
      "config": {
        "variant": "secondary",
        "goToStep": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "btn-search-ap",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "search('ap') ✗",
      "config": {
        "variant": "destructive",
        "goToStep": 6
      }
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 1",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "insert('app')  →  a → p → p*",
      "canvas": {
        "trie-tree": {
          "nodeStates": {
            "a1": { "highlight": "active" },
            "p1": { "highlight": "active" },
            "p2": { "highlight": "found" }
          },
          "newNodes": [
            { "id": "a1", "value": "a", "children": ["p1"], "isEnd": false },
            { "id": "p1", "value": "p", "children": ["p2"], "isEnd": false },
            { "id": "p2", "value": "p*", "children": [], "isEnd": true }
          ],
          "updateNodes": [
            { "id": "root", "children": ["a1"] }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Prefix Sharing",
        "body": "\"apple\" and \"app\" share the path `a → p → p`. Only the suffix diverges.\n\nThis sharing makes Tries memory-efficient for large dictionaries with common prefixes — like all English words starting with \"pre\" or \"un\".",
        "callout": "A 50,000-word English dictionary uses far fewer nodes than 50,000 strings stored separately."
      },
      "activeText": "insert('apple')  →  shared prefix 'app' + new l → e*",
      "canvas": {
        "trie-tree": {
          "nodeStates": {
            "l1": { "highlight": "active" },
            "e1": { "highlight": "found" }
          },
          "newNodes": [
            { "id": "l1", "value": "l", "children": ["e1"], "isEnd": false },
            { "id": "e1", "value": "e*", "children": [], "isEnd": true }
          ],
          "updateNodes": [
            { "id": "p2", "children": ["l1"] }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 3",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "insert('ban')  →  new branch: b → a → n*  (no shared prefix)",
      "canvas": {
        "trie-tree": {
          "nodeStates": {
            "b1": { "highlight": "active" },
            "an1": { "highlight": "active" },
            "n1": { "highlight": "found" }
          },
          "newNodes": [
            { "id": "b1", "value": "b", "children": ["an1"], "isEnd": false },
            { "id": "an1", "value": "a", "children": ["n1"], "isEnd": false },
            { "id": "n1", "value": "n*", "children": [], "isEnd": true }
          ],
          "updateNodes": [
            { "id": "root", "children": ["a1", "b1"] }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 4",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "search('app')  →  traverse root→a→p→p*  →  found (word end)  ✓",
      "canvas": {
        "trie-tree": {
          "nodeStates": {
            "root": { "highlight": "found" },
            "a1": { "highlight": "found" },
            "p1": { "highlight": "found" },
            "p2": { "highlight": "found" }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "search() vs startsWith()",
        "body": "**search(word)**: traverse character by character. Return true only if you reach the end AND the last node has `isEnd = true`.\n\n**startsWith(prefix)**: same traversal, but return true as soon as the path exists — `isEnd` doesn't matter.\n\nBoth are O(m) where m = length of the query."
      },
      "activeText": "startsWith('ap')  →  traverse root→a→p  →  prefix exists  ✓",
      "canvas": {
        "trie-tree": {
          "nodeStates": {
            "root": { "highlight": "found" },
            "a1": { "highlight": "found" },
            "p1": { "highlight": "found" }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "search('ap') → false, startsWith('ap') → true",
        "body": "The node `p` at depth 2 exists — so `startsWith('ap')` is true.\n\nBut `p` at depth 2 has `isEnd = false` — 'ap' was never inserted as a complete word. So `search('ap')` is false."
      },
      "activeText": "search('ap')  →  traverse root→a→p  →  p is NOT a word end  →  false",
      "canvas": {
        "trie-tree": {
          "nodeStates": {
            "root": { "highlight": "active" },
            "a1": { "highlight": "active" }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 7",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "insert('banana')  →  extends 'ban' with a→n→a*",
      "canvas": {
        "trie-tree": {
          "nodeStates": {
            "na1": { "highlight": "active" },
            "nan1": { "highlight": "active" },
            "nana1": { "highlight": "found" }
          },
          "newNodes": [
            { "id": "na1", "value": "a", "children": ["nan1"], "isEnd": false },
            { "id": "nan1", "value": "n", "children": ["nana1"], "isEnd": false },
            { "id": "nana1", "value": "a*", "children": [], "isEnd": true }
          ],
          "updateNodes": [
            { "id": "n1", "children": ["na1"] }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 8",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "search('xyz')  →  'x' not a child of root  →  immediately false  (O(m))",
      "canvas": {
        "trie-tree": {}
      }
    }
  ],
  "popups": [
    {
      "id": "pop-shared-prefix",
      "attachTo": "trie-tree",
      "text": "Shared prefix! apple re-uses app's path",
      "showAtStep": 2,
      "hideAtStep": 3,
      "style": "insight"
    },
    {
      "id": "pop-word-end",
      "attachTo": "trie-tree",
      "text": "* = isEnd marker. search() requires this.",
      "showAtStep": 4,
      "hideAtStep": 6,
      "style": "info"
    }
  ],
  "challenges": [
    {
      "id": "ch-autocomplete",
      "title": "Build Autocomplete",
      "description": "Using the Trie structure, design an autocomplete function: given a prefix string, return all words that start with that prefix. What's the time complexity? How would you limit results to the top 5 most frequent words?",
      "type": "optimize"
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-delete-word",
      "title": "Delete a Word",
      "description": "Deleting a word from a Trie is tricky — you can't just remove the nodes because other words might share them. Design the delete algorithm. When can you safely delete a node, and when must you only clear the isEnd flag?",
      "type": "scenario"
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-count-prefixes",
      "title": "Count Words with Prefix",
      "description": "Add a `countStartsWith(prefix)` function that counts how many inserted words start with a given prefix. What extra state would you store in each node to make this O(m) instead of O(n)?",
      "type": "optimize"
    }
  ]
}
